Context
Complaint statuses follow strict transitions (New → In Progress → Resolved → Closed). Different tenants may extend workflows in future. Hard-coding these transitions spreads logic across controllers and services.

Decision
Introduce a Workflow Engine component responsible for validating and executing complaint state transitions.

Rationale
Centralises business rules
Prevents invalid transitions (e.g., Closed → New)
Supports audits and SLA recalculation during transitions
Easily extendable for future complexity

Consequences
All state changes must pass through the engine
Extra abstraction layer but improves maintainability
Requires clear configuration for allowed transitions
Alternatives Considered
Hard-coding transitions in the service → brittle and duplicated
Storing transitions in DB → too complex for initial implementation
